Article 11: Where a shareholder of a foreign-invested enterprise transfers all or part of its equity to a third party other than the shareholders, the unanimous consent of the other shareholders shall be obtained. Where the other shareholders request revocation of the equity transfer contract on the ground that their consent was not obtained, the People's Court shall support it, except in any of the following circumstances:
(1) There is evidence proving that the other shareholders have already consented;
(2) The transferor has given written notice of the equity transfer, and the other shareholders have failed to reply within thirty days from the date of receipt of the written notice;
(3) The other shareholders do not consent to the transfer and also do not purchase the transferred equity.

Article 14: Where the parties agree that one party makes actual investment and the other party serves as the nominal shareholder of a foreign-invested enterprise, and the actual investor requests confirmation of its shareholder status in the foreign-invested enterprise or requests a change of shareholders of the foreign-invested enterprise, the People's Court shall not support it, except where all of the following conditions are met:
(1) The actual investor has already made actual investment;
(2) Shareholders other than the nominal shareholder recognize the shareholder status of the actual investor;
(3) The People's Court or the parties have obtained consent from the examination and approval authority for foreign-invested enterprises during the litigation period to change the actual investor to a shareholder.
